# Known answers for the campaign walk: 48 distinguished-point records written
# by the ecc2k-130 campaign's own client, github.com/aburan28/crypto ecc2k130
# (commit 803c99b81cf5), CPU build, from Certicom's challenge points:
#
#   ecc2k130-cpu --curve 131 --run-id 4321 --dp-weight 46 --threads 4 \
#                --steps 256 --launches 8 --dp-file kat.bin --verify 20
#
# every 350th of the 16839 records it wrote (21 of these 48 on a restarted
# seed, low 16 bits nonzero).  One 32-byte record per line, in hex, exactly as
# the corpus file holds it: little-endian seed, then the orbit-minimum x.
# Weight 46 because a point at the campaign's 32 is 2^28 steps away; the
# cutoff is a parameter of the walk, not a different rule.  hosttest walks
# every seed from the challenge points on fpga/model and requires the same
# 32 bytes back.
